---
import FigureHeading from '../FigureHeading.astro';
import ModelTraceExcerpt from './ModelTraceExcerpt.astro';

const breaks = [
  {
    id: 'constraint',
    stage: 'Task specification',
    label: 'Constraint drift',
    description: 'one-sided bound → invented interval',
    trace: 'Cathepsin_K_20 · Kimi',
    kind: 'fork',
  },
  {
    id: 'identity',
    stage: 'Candidate',
    label: 'Candidate mix-up',
    description: 'one name → two molecules',
    trace: 'CYP1B1_0 · Qwen',
    kind: 'alias',
  },
  {
    id: 'borderline',
    stage: 'Evidence',
    label: 'Borderline oracle',
    description: 'one call → treated as certainty',
    trace: 'DHODH_12 · Claude',
    kind: 'threshold',
  },
  {
    id: 'known-fail',
    stage: 'Decision',
    label: 'Evidence ignored',
    description: 'known failure → submitted',
    trace: 'DHODH_14 · Kimi',
    kind: 'bypass',
  },
  {
    id: 'finalist',
    stage: 'Submission',
    label: 'Finalist not verified',
    description: 'exact finalist → unverified',
    trace: 'CDK2_20 · Claude',
    kind: 'missing',
  },
];
---

<lo-failure-map id="lo-failure-map">
  <figure aria-label="Five observed points where state broke in Lead Optimization trajectories">
    <FigureHeading label="FIG. 13" title="Where agent state breaks down" />

    <div class="figure-meta">
      <b>inspect a failure</b>
    </div>
    <p class="dek">Useful chemistry could survive while the state around it became inconsistent.</p>

    <div class="map-scroll">
      <nav class="break-map" aria-label="Select a trajectory break">
        {breaks.map((item) => (
          <button
            type="button"
            data-mode-button={item.id}
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="failure-detail"
          >
            <span class="stage">{item.stage}</span>
            <span class:list={['disturbance', item.kind]} aria-hidden="true">
              <i></i><b></b><em></em>
            </span>
            <strong>{item.label}</strong>
            <span class="description">{item.description}</span>
            <small>{item.trace}</small>
          </button>
        ))}
      </nav>
    </div>

    <p class="resting-note"><span aria-hidden="true">↑</span> select a break to inspect the trajectory</p>

    <div id="failure-detail" class="detail-region" aria-live="polite" hidden>
      <section class="story constraint-story" data-story="constraint" hidden>
        <header class="story-heading">
          <div><span class="story-index">01</span><h3>The requirement changed while the search was running.</h3></div>
          <p>Kimi K2.5 · Cathepsin_K_20 · turns 23–24</p>
        </header>

        <div class="requirement-mutation">
          <article>
            <span>Task prompt</span>
            <strong>solubility ≥ −5.3183</strong>
            <small>one-sided lower bound</small>
          </article>
          <div class="mutation-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><i>→</i><b>new boundary</b></div>
          <article class="model-range">
            <span>Model · turn 23</span>
            <strong>[−5.3183, −4.3183]</strong>
            <small>invented two-sided interval</small>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="numberline-comparison">
          <article class="numberline actual">
            <header><span>Task gate</span><strong>pass</strong></header>
            <div class="axis"><span class="allowed"></span><i class="lower"></i><b class="point"></b></div>
            <div class="axis-labels"><span>−5.3183</span><strong>candidate −3.8493</strong></div>
          </article>
          <article class="numberline believed">
            <header><span>Model’s gate</span><strong>“too high”</strong></header>
            <div class="axis"><span class="allowed"></span><i class="lower"></i><i class="upper"></i><b class="point"></b></div>
            <div class="axis-labels"><span>−5.3183</span><em>−4.3183</em><strong>candidate −3.8493</strong></div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <ModelTraceExcerpt
          model="Kimi K2.5"
          excerpts={[
            {
              turn: 'turn 23',
              text: 'This methylpiperazine_sulf candidate is very promising: clearance … ✓; ames … ✓; hERG … ✓; BBB … ✓; solubility: −3.849 … ✗.',
            },
            {
              turn: 'turn 24',
              text: 'Solubility: −3.849 … outside −5.318 to −4.318 — too high.',
              warning: true,
            },
          ]}
        />
        <p class="scene-caption">The candidate satisfied the stated directional bound. It failed only after the task specification drifted inside the model’s working state.</p>

        <button class="turns-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">view surrounding turns <span>↓</span></button>
        <ol class="surrounding-turns" hidden>
          <li class="task-turn">
            <b>T00</b><span>task</span>
            <div><strong>Original requirement</strong><p>Keep solubility within 0.5 of the −4.8183 baseline, with a decrease tolerance. The operative lower bound was −5.3183.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn">
            <b>T22</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>Searching for a better trade-off</strong><p>“The thiomorpholine has very good Ames (0.503), good hERG (0.29), but clearance is 95.89—too high.” The model pivots to the methylpiperazine candidate.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T22</b><span>tool</span>
            <div><strong>ADMET · methylpiperazine_sulf</strong><dl><div><dt>clearance</dt><dd>66.7542</dd></div><div><dt>Ames</dt><dd>0.5438</dd></div><div><dt>hERG</dt><dd>0.3210</dd></div><div><dt>BBB</dt><dd>0.5402</dd></div><div class="failed"><dt>solubility</dt><dd>−3.8493</dd></div></dl></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn">
            <b>T23</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>Four passes, then a rejection</strong><p>“This methylpiperazine_sulf candidate is very promising.” It marks clearance, Ames, hERG, and BBB as passes, then computes solubility as 0.969 from baseline and marks it ✗—because it has silently converted the directional tolerance into a symmetric interval.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn critical-turn">
            <b>T24</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>The invented upper boundary becomes state</strong><p>It writes the target as “−5.318 to −4.318,” calls −3.849 “too high,” and decides to add F, Cl, or other hydrophobic groups to lower solubility. The subsequent search is now optimizing against the model’s rewritten requirement.</p></div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="story identity-story" data-story="identity" hidden>
        <header class="story-heading">
          <div><span class="story-index">02</span><h3>The alias stayed fixed. The molecule underneath it did not.</h3></div>
          <p>Qwen 3.5 397B-A17B · CYP1B1_0 · turns 6–22</p>
        </header>

        <div class="alias-diagram">
          <div class="alias-token"><span>alias</span><strong>“c4”</strong><i aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
          <article class="molecule-card molecule-a">
            <header><span>Turn 6 · molecule A</span><small>generated as “c4”</small></header>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 300 130" role="img" aria-label="First molecular graph called c4">
              <g class="bonds">
                <polygon points="22,66 41,34 78,34 97,66 78,98 41,98" />
                <line x1="31" y1="65" x2="47" y2="39" /><line x1="73" y1="41" x2="88" y2="66" /><line x1="72" y1="91" x2="46" y2="91" />
                <line x1="97" y1="66" x2="126" y2="66" />
                <polygon points="126,66 144,39 176,48 181,80 151,95" />
                <line x1="181" y1="66" x2="204" y2="66" />
                <polygon points="204,66 223,34 260,34 279,66 260,98 223,98" />
                <line x1="213" y1="65" x2="229" y2="39" /><line x1="255" y1="41" x2="270" y2="66" /><line x1="254" y1="91" x2="228" y2="91" />
              </g>
              <g class="atoms"><text x="8" y="29">HO</text><text x="261" y="29">OMe</text><text x="259" y="116">MeO</text><text x="139" y="41">N</text><text x="153" y="99">S</text></g>
            </svg>
            <p><span>evidence attached</span><b>similarity 0.85</b></p>
          </article>
          <article class="molecule-card molecule-b">
            <header><span>Turn 9 · molecule B</span><small>tested as “c4”</small></header>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 300 130" role="img" aria-label="Second molecular graph called c4">
              <g class="bonds">
                <polygon points="22,66 41,34 78,34 97,66 78,98 41,98" />
                <line x1="31" y1="65" x2="47" y2="39" /><line x1="73" y1="41" x2="88" y2="66" /><line x1="72" y1="91" x2="46" y2="91" />
                <line x1="97" y1="66" x2="126" y2="66" />
                <polygon points="126,66 144,39 176,48 181,80 151,95" />
                <line x1="181" y1="66" x2="204" y2="66" />
                <polygon points="204,66 223,34 260,34 279,66 260,98 223,98" />
                <line x1="213" y1="65" x2="229" y2="39" /><line x1="255" y1="41" x2="270" y2="66" /><line x1="254" y1="91" x2="228" y2="91" />
              </g>
              <g class="atoms"><text x="8" y="29">HO</text><text x="39" y="119">MeO</text><text x="261" y="29">OH</text><text x="139" y="41">N</text><text x="153" y="99">S</text></g>
            </svg>
            <p><span>evidence attached</span><b>ADMET · Boltz 0.875</b></p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="mixed-evidence">
          <span>“c4” evidence</span><i>similarity 0.85</i><i>ADMET passes</i><i>Boltz 0.875</i><b>but exact graph similarity = 0.683</b>
        </div>
        <ModelTraceExcerpt
          model="Qwen 3.5 397B-A17B"
          excerpts={[
            {
              turn: 'turn 8',
              text: 'Candidates that have similarity ≥ 0.7: c1: Sim=0.74; c4: Sim=0.85. Let me test these candidates.',
            },
            {
              turn: 'turn 22',
              text: 'c4 had similarity 0.85 but the canonical form showed 0.68.',
              warning: true,
            },
          ]}
        />
        <p class="scene-caption">Evidence from two molecular graphs was carried under one name. The contradiction appeared only when molecule B was rechecked exactly.</p>

        <button class="turns-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">view surrounding turns <span>↓</span></button>
        <ol class="surrounding-turns" hidden>
          <li class="model-turn">
            <b>T06</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>Candidate family is defined</strong><p>The model proposes converting aromatic methoxy groups to hydroxyls to lower LogP, increase solubility, and reduce BBB penetration. It assigns short aliases—including <code>c4</code>—to the generated graphs.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn">
            <b>T08</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>The first graph receives the label</strong><p>“Candidates that have similarity ≥ 0.7: c1: Sim=0.74; c4: Sim=0.85.” At this point, <code>c4</code> refers to the higher-similarity generated molecule.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T09</b><span>tool</span>
            <div><strong>Different graph, same alias</strong><p><code>predict_admet</code> is called on a hydroxyl-bearing graph recorded as <code>c4</code>. It returns hERG 0.4296, BBB 0.1452, solubility −4.4246, and CYP3A4 0.8269. Those results remain attached to the alias.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T15</b><span>tool</span>
            <div><strong>Binding evidence joins the mixed record</strong><p>The second graph is passed to Boltz under <code>c4</code>. It returns binding probability 0.874583 and affinity −1.137927, reinforcing confidence in the aliased candidate.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn critical-turn">
            <b>T22</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>Exact recomputation exposes the collision</strong><p>“The similarity is 0.683, which is below 0.7 … c4 had similarity 0.85 but the canonical form showed 0.68.” The same name now carries the similarity of molecule A and the ADMET/Boltz evidence of molecule B.</p></div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="story borderline-story" data-story="borderline" hidden>
        <header class="story-heading">
          <div><span class="story-index">03</span><h3>One sample was treated as a distribution.</h3></div>
          <p>Claude Sonnet 4.6 · DHODH_12 · turn 8</p>
        </header>

        <div class="threshold-plot">
          <div class="threshold-heading"><span>Boltz affinity · turn 8</span><strong>required ≤ −1.637547</strong></div>
          <div class="threshold-axis"><span class="pass-region"></span><i class="cutoff"></i><b class="trajectory-point"></b><b class="evaluator-point"></b></div>
          <div class="threshold-label trajectory"><span>observed</span><strong>−1.652409</strong><small>pass</small></div>
          <div class="threshold-label evaluator"><span>official evaluation</span><strong>−1.6372</strong><small>fail</small></div>
        </div>

        <div class="sample-budget">
          <div><span class="used">●</span>{Array.from({ length: 7 }).map(() => <span>○</span>)}</div>
          <p><strong>Boltz budget after this call</strong><small>7 calls remained · nothing was sampled again</small></p>
        </div>
        <ModelTraceExcerpt
          model="Claude Sonnet 4.6"
          excerpts={[
            {
              turn: 'turn 6',
              text: 'The results look promising. mod5 … passes all ADMET constraints. Let me extract the protein sequence and run Boltz prediction.',
            },
            {
              turn: 'turn 10',
              text: 'All constraints are satisfied … Binding probability: 0.933 > 0.7 … Affinity: −1.652 (diff 0.285 ≤ 0.3).',
              warning: true,
            },
          ]}
        />
        <p class="scene-caption">The observed margin was smaller than the variation between trajectory and evaluator calls, yet the single passing prediction was treated as certainty.</p>

        <button class="turns-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">view surrounding turns <span>↓</span></button>
        <ol class="surrounding-turns" hidden>
          <li class="model-turn">
            <b>T06</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>A promising candidate is promoted</strong><p>“mod5 (pyrazole CH₂OH) passes all ADMET constraints,” with solubility improved by about 1.07 and the remaining properties within tolerance. The model moves directly to a binding check.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T08</b><span>Boltz</span>
            <div><strong>One prediction lands just inside the gate</strong><dl><div><dt>affinity</dt><dd>−1.652409</dd></div><div><dt>required</dt><dd>≤ −1.637547</dd></div><div><dt>margin</dt><dd>0.014862</dd></div><div><dt>probability</dt><dd>0.932830</dd></div><div><dt>calls left</dt><dd>7</dd></div></dl></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T09</b><span>tool</span>
            <div><strong>Deterministic checks all pass</strong><p>MW 456.5, LogP 3.58, TPSA 98.4, Tanimoto 0.922, SA 3.10, and the PAINS/Brenk filters are verified. The report repeats the single Boltz value but does not test its stability.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn critical-turn">
            <b>T10</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>A sample becomes a fact</strong><p>“All constraints are satisfied.” The checklist records affinity −1.652 with a difference of 0.285 ≤ 0.3 and binding probability 0.933, but contains no uncertainty estimate, repeat call, or acknowledgement that the margin is only 0.0149.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T10</b><span>write</span>
            <div><strong>Search ends with budget unused</strong><p>The model writes <code>solution.smi</code>. Seven Boltz calls remain available; none are used to replicate the borderline result.</p></div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="story known-story" data-story="known-fail" hidden>
        <header class="story-heading">
          <div><span class="story-index">04</span><h3>The agent wrote “fail,” then submitted the same molecule.</h3></div>
          <p>Kimi K2.5 · DHODH_14 · turns 46–48</p>
        </header>

        <div class="trace-timeline">
          <article>
            <header><span>Turn 46</span><b>tool</b></header>
            <dl><div><dt>hERG</dt><dd>0.6648975</dd></div><div><dt>required</dt><dd>≤ 0.663</dd></div></dl>
          </article>
          <i class="time-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</i>
          <article class="model-fragment">
            <header><span>Turn 46</span><b>model</b></header>
            <q>FAIL (out by 0.002)</q>
          </article>
          <i class="time-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</i>
          <article class="submit-fragment">
            <header><span>Turn 48</span><b>submit</b></header>
            <strong>same molecule</strong>
            <code>CCC[C@H](C)Oc1cc(…N(C)C…)ccc1C</code>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="broken-evidence" aria-label="Known failure did not reach submission"><span>known fail</span><i></i><b></b><i></i><span>submitted</span></div>
        <ModelTraceExcerpt
          model="Kimi K2.5"
          excerpts={[
            {
              turn: 'turn 37',
              text: 'NMe2-meta: All hard constraints pass, 4/5 ADMET good, but hERG is 0.665 vs target 0.663 (out by 0.002).',
              warning: true,
            },
            {
              turn: 'turn 47',
              text: 'Even though binding probability is below 0.7, this is the best candidate found … Let me write the solution file with the best candidate found.',
              warning: true,
            },
          ]}
        />
        <p class="scene-caption">This is visible in adjacent trace events: the failure was explicit, but the evidence did not survive into the final decision.</p>

        <button class="turns-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">view surrounding turns <span>↓</span></button>
        <ol class="surrounding-turns" hidden>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T29</b><span>ADMET</span>
            <div><strong>The disqualifying result first appears</strong><dl><div class="failed"><dt>hERG</dt><dd>0.664898</dd></div><div><dt>allowed</dt><dd>0.463–0.663</dd></div><div><dt>BBB</dt><dd>0.477697</dd></div><div><dt>CYP3A4</dt><dd>0.598056</dd></div><div><dt>clearance</dt><dd>54.0797</dd></div></dl></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn">
            <b>T30</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>The first comparison is internally inconsistent</strong><p>It calls the candidate “very promising” and writes: “hERG: 0.665 … target range: 0.463–0.663 ✓ — within 0.102, just barely at edge.” The arithmetic exceeds both the upper bound and the stated ±0.1 tolerance, despite the checkmark.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn">
            <b>T31</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>The model notices the miss</strong><p>“The hERG is slightly out of range (0.665 vs acceptable range 0.463–0.663). I need to reduce hERG slightly.” It proposes F, Cl, CF₃, and ester substitutions and continues searching.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn">
            <b>T37</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>Known failure becomes an accepted compromise</strong><p>The model compares NMe2-meta—hERG out by 0.002—with F-meta—BBB out by 0.029—and decides “the NMe2 candidate is closer to target.” Closeness has silently replaced the requirement to pass every gate.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn critical-turn">
            <b>T46</b><span>verify</span>
            <div><strong>The final ledger still contains two explicit failures</strong><dl><div><dt>hard constraints</dt><dd>pass</dd></div><div class="failed"><dt>hERG</dt><dd>0.665 · fail</dd></div><div class="failed"><dt>Boltz probability</dt><dd>0.507 · fail</dd></div><div><dt>reference probability</dt><dd>0.389</dd></div></dl><p>The verification says the result is “below 0.7” and that hERG is “out by 0.002.”</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="model-turn critical-turn">
            <b>T47</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>The same molecule is selected anyway</strong><p>“Even though binding probability is below 0.7, this is the best candidate found.” It also notes “NMe2-meta: binding 0.507, ADMET known, hERG slightly off,” then writes that exact candidate to <code>solution.smi</code>.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T48</b><span>submit</span>
            <div><strong>File acceptance is not constraint success</strong><p>The submission call again states hERG is 0.002 out of tolerance and binding probability is 0.507 versus the required 0.7. The harness responds only: “Submission accepted: solution.smi.”</p></div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="story finalist-story" data-story="finalist" hidden>
        <header class="story-heading">
          <div><span class="story-index">05</span><h3>The exact finalist had an incomplete evidence record.</h3></div>
          <p>Claude Sonnet 4.6 · CDK2_20 · turns 32–35</p>
        </header>

        <div class="finalist-layout">
          <article class="finalist-candidate">
            <span>Exact finalist</span>
            <strong>3,4-diol</strong>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 170 105" role="img" aria-label="Simplified diagram of final 3,4-diol candidate">
              <g><polygon points="20,53 39,21 76,21 95,53 76,85 39,85"/><line x1="95" y1="53" x2="125" y2="53"/><polygon points="125,53 142,29 161,53 142,77"/></g>
              <text x="27" y="18">HO</text><text x="68" y="101">OH</text><text x="137" y="28">N</text>
            </svg>
            <code>CC(C)(C)c1cnc(…[C@H](O)[C@H](O)…)</code>
          </article>

          <article class="evidence-ledger">
            <header><span>Evidence ledger</span><small>exact molecule only</small></header>
            <dl>
              <div class="measured"><dt>Boltz</dt><dd><b>✓ measured</b><small>turn 32 · affinity −2.091</small></dd></div>
              <div class="measured"><dt>Structural checks</dt><dd><b>✓ measured</b><small>turn 33 · all pass</small></dd></div>
              <div class="missing"><dt>ADMET</dt><dd><b>— missing</b><small>budget exhausted before this edit</small></dd></div>
              <div class="missing"><dt>BBB</dt><dd><b>— missing</b><small>inferred from earlier analogues</small></dd></div>
            </dl>
          </article>

          <div class="submit-result">
            <span class="submit-arrow">submit →</span>
            <article><span>Official evaluator</span><strong>BBB 0.66895</strong><small>required ≥ 0.6744</small><b>fail</b></article>
          </div>
        </div>

        <ModelTraceExcerpt
          model="Claude Sonnet 4.6"
          excerpts={[
            {
              turn: 'turn 33',
              text: 'Excellent! The 3,4-diOH cyclohexyl variant gives … affinity: −2.091 … binding probability: 0.975. Let me verify this compound satisfies all hard constraints and ADMET.',
            },
            {
              turn: 'turn 34',
              text: 'The key question is the ADMET constraints. Let me estimate based on what we know … BBB might decrease slightly with increased TPSA. Let me write the solution.',
              warning: true,
            },
          ]}
        />
        <p class="scene-caption">A nearby molecule’s evidence was not evidence for the exact finalist. The last edit created a new candidate with empty ledger slots.</p>

        <button class="turns-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false">view surrounding turns <span>↓</span></button>
        <ol class="surrounding-turns" hidden>
          <li class="model-turn">
            <b>T31</b><span>model</span>
            <div><strong>Two binding calls remain; ADMET is exhausted</strong><p>The current 2Me-cyclohexanol candidate has 0.963 binding probability but misses the required affinity improvement. The model reasons that an extra hydroxyl could add a protein hydrogen bond while retaining Tanimoto similarity, then spends a remaining Boltz call on the 3,4-diol.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T32</b><span>Boltz</span>
            <div><strong>The new finalist wins on binding</strong><dl><div><dt>affinity</dt><dd>−2.090998</dd></div><div><dt>improvement</dt><dd>0.446397</dd></div><div><dt>probability</dt><dd>0.975109</dd></div><div><dt>calls left</dt><dd>1</dd></div></dl><p>The call rationale predicts that the added hydroxyl may interact with HIS82, HIS84, or ASP145.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="tool-turn">
            <b>T33</b><span>verify</span>
